--TEST--
A route method's parameter that a path capture names cannot also have `#[Core\Query]`: one parameter gets one value, from the path or from the query string — `rule:routing/a-query-parameter-is-declared-like-a-capture`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Shop {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/orders/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(#[Core\Query] uint $id): string {
        return "";
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E1009]: `$id` is filled by the capture `{id}` of the path, so it cannot also be a `#[Query]` parameter
  --> case.nvs:5:26
%A
  = help: delete `#[Core\Query]` to read `$id` from the path, or delete `{id}` from the path to read it from the query string

